print("Welcome to practice questions about loops!\nBy: Sophia Luo\n--------------------------\n1. What keys can you press if your Python program is stuck in an infinite loop?\nJust press the stop button!\n--------------------\n2. What is the difference between break and continue?\nBreak is to completely stop the program, while continue is to skip some, like \"end = \" \"\"\n--------------------------\n3. What is the difference between range(10), range(0, 10), and range(0, 10, 1) in a for loop?\n \"range(10)\" as a loop means to print it 10 times\n\"range(0, 10)\" means the same as the last one, but instead it starts at the first number, like 0\n\"range(0, 10, 2)\" means to print it, but it skips 2, like first 0, then 2\n-----------------\n4. Write a short program that prints the numbers 1 to 10 using a for loop. Then, write an equivalent program that prints the numbers 1 to 10 using a while loop.\nAvailiable in other code called 'Practice Questions chap4.code q4.py'\n--------------------\n5. If you had a function named bacon() inside a module named spam, how would you call it after importing spam?\n It is \"spam.bacon()\"\n-------------------\nThe End")